{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>A fruitful branch is Joseph.</b> 'Branch' (בן) is like 'shoot' and it is in the feminine, as in 'you have adopted' (עַל־בֵּן אִמָּצְתָּ לְךָ, Psalm 80:16). The grammatical analysis of פֹּרָת is feminine active, for the active participle is found in two forms, like אֹיְבֶיהָ and אֹיַבְתִּי, and likewise פֹּרֶה and פֹּרָת, from the language of 'fruitful' (פּוֹרִיָּה, Psalm 128:3). Some interpret it from the language of 'and it sent out branches' (וְתִשְׁלַח פַּאֲרוֹת, Ezekiel 17:6). And he mentioned 'fruitful branch' (בן פורת) twice, in the manner of the speakers of the holy language: 'For lo, Your enemies, YHWH, for lo, Your enemies' (Psalm 92:9), the meaning being time after time, constantly. And according to the second interpretation the tav [in פורת] is the feminine marker [as] one [word], like the tav of 'and it ceased [for] the prince' (וְשָׁבַת לַנָּשִׂיא, Ezekiel 46:17)." "<b>And the meaning of 'daughters stepped upon the wall' (בְּנוֹת צָעֲדָה עֲלֵי שׁוּר).</b> That Joseph was like a fruitful branch (בן פרת), and produced daughters — stepped (צעדה), each and every one of them, upon the wall. And the meaning is that they grew exceedingly tall over the fortified walls, 'daughters stepped,' in the manner of 'dead flies cause [ointment] to stink' (זְבוּבֵי מָוֶת יַבְאִישׁ, Ecclesiastes 10:1)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "Resolved the abbreviated grammatical term 'תדת ח\"א' as 'the feminine marker [as] one [word]' based on context; reading uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:40.873990050Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}